# GitHub runner slots on intent-ci3, a runner-only host (no cache services):
# AMD EPYC 4545P, 16 cores / 32 threads, 64 GB. See docs/GITHUB_RUNNERS.md,
# "Add a runner host". Not secret. Install with:
#   infra/runners/install.sh --config infra/runners/hosts/intent-ci3.env
GITHUB_ORG=intent-hq
RUNNER_GROUP=intent-cache
RUNNER_GROUP_REPOS=intent,intentd,cloudlands-fe
RUNNER_NAME_PREFIX=intent-ci3
RUNNER_POOLS=heavy

# CPU n and n+16 are SMT siblings (Linux numbers every core's first thread,
# then every second thread; install.sh checks thread_siblings_list). No xl
# slot: intent-ci1 and intent-ci2 serve the xl pool.

# Heavy pool: four 8-thread slots, two per CCD (cores 0-3, 4-7 on CCD 0;
# 8-11, 12-15 on CCD 1), each with both SMT siblings of its cores. Every core
# is pinned. Memory: 4 x 12 GB = 48 GB, under the 51G runners.slice cap (the
# box reports 60 GiB of its 64 GB, minus 9), leaving about 12 GiB for the
# system and Docker. Smaller than the 30-36 GB heavy slots elsewhere: if jobs
# here are OOM-killed, drop to three slots (HEAVY_SLOTS=3, HEAVY_MEMORY=16g).
HEAVY_SLOTS=4
HEAVY_LABELS=self-hosted,linux,x64,intent-cache
HEAVY_CPUSETS=0-3,16-19 4-7,20-23 8-11,24-27 12-15,28-31
HEAVY_MEMORY=12g
HEAVY_PIDS=16384
HEAVY_SHM=1g
